{"input":"Executable task contract:\nJSON scalar values in this task are null, boolean, integer (excluding boolean), or string. No floating point or coercion is used. Scalar equality is type-sensitive. Malformed tasks are outside the valid-task domain.\nInput: `events` is a list of `{key:string,version:nonnegative_integer,at:nonnegative_integer,op:\"put\"|\"delete\",value:JSON_scalar}`; delete events have value null. Events may appear out of chronological order and repeated versions may conflict. `queries` is an ordered list of `{query_id:string,key:string,as_of:nonnegative_integer}` with distinct query IDs. For each query independently, consider only events for the exact key with at<=as_of. Choose the event with greatest tuple (version,at,zero_based_input_event_index), so a later lower version cannot replace a higher eligible version; same-version conflicts use chronological time then input order. An eligible higher-version tombstone remains authoritative over lower versions. If no eligible event exists, return status=\"absent\", value=null, chosen_version=null, chosen_event=null. For a selected delete return status=\"deleted\", value=null and its version/index. For a selected put return status=\"present\", its exact value and version/index, including present null values. Return exactly `{results:[{query_id,key,status,value,chosen_version,chosen_event}]}` in query order. Entries for other keys and future events are irrelevant. This task is bounded versioned retrieval, not evidence of a learned long-term memory system.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"episodic\",\"events\":[{\"key\":\"panel\",\"version\":5,\"at\":28,\"op\":\"put\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"cabinet\",\"version\":113,\"at\":18,\"op\":\"put\",\"value\":\"jade\"},{\"key\":\"panel\",\"version\":2,\"at\":24,\"op\":\"put\",\"value\":\"cobalt\"},{\"key\":\"bridge\",\"version\":2,\"at\":7,\"op\":\"put\",\"value\":\"violet\"},{\"key\":\"panel\",\"version\":4,\"at\":27,\"op\":\"delete\",\"value\":null},{\"key\":\"bri